KG42.register("nodes-9897e0f5fd306997ba2d532c",{"id":"KG31-84de1f1af39d310b","code":"PRC019.2","label":"Separate purchase and sale pricing maximizing operator profit","definition":"Treats the unit prices on the internal purchase and sale sides as a joint decision, maximizing the operator's profit in combination with participant price response, external surplus-deficit trading, and price constraints, thereby forming an optimal price pair shared by each side within the region.","layer":"L6","template_code":"PGR","concept_id":"pricing.local","concept_ids":["pricing.local"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Function: jointly optimize to generate internal purchase and sale prices","Price structure: the internal purchase side and sale side each share one price","Economic principle: maximization of operator profit accounting for consumption response and external balance trading"]},"exclusions":[["The MGO simultaneously selects p_b and p_s to maximize R(p_b,p_s); the main-text constraint is λ^s≤p_s\u003cp_b≤λ^b.","When E^s>E^b, R=p_bE^b−p_sE^s+λ^s(E^s−E^b); otherwise R=p_bE^b−p_sE^s+λ^b(E^s−E^b).","D_1 corresponds to E^b\u003cE^s, and D_2 corresponds to E^b≥E^s; comparing the profits at the optimal points in the two domains determines (p_b^*,p_s^*).","Implementation may use an interior-point method and broadcast the price for the next time slot; transaction quantities adopt the source text's price response.","The extreme-value response in equation (2) requires E_n^g−x_n≠0, and the consumption strategy has separate upper and lower bounds.","Initial prices may be set to p_s=λ^s and p_b=λ^b; the case grid prices are 0.4 and 1.0 CNY/kWh.","The strict price spread in the main text, another upper bound on λ^b_n, and the non-strict two-sided bounds in the appendix are retained separately and are not uniformly rewritten.","In the case, during shortage in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, p_s is raised; during surplus in 13 and 14, p_b is lowered; this is not extended into a general adjustment algorithm.","In the case, when there is no internally tradable electricity in time slots 7 and 17-19, the prices remain at the grid prices."]],"members":[{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"The MGO coordinates and optimizes local PV energy sharing with the objective of maximizing its own profit. Scope: Hour-ahead energy-sharing management among PV prosumers within one microgrid. The internal prices p_b and p_s determine the aggregate trading quantities E^b and E^s through the model's price-dependent consumption responses. Scope: Determination of aggregate local trading quantities in the Stackelberg energy-sharing model. Condition: Trading quantities use the consumption response in (2), derived under E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0. The final ESM decision may be scheduled five minutes before the time slot. Scope: Implementation timing of the final local energy-sharing decision for a forthcoming time slot. Condition: The monitoring and control system's communication latency is commonly less than several seconds.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Determination of aggregate local trading quantities in the Stackelberg energy-sharing model. | Hour-ahead energy-sharing management among PV prosumers within one microgrid. | Implementation timing of the final local energy-sharing decision for a forthcoming time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E06"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C004"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"3a304bae600d1d987d8d474ca346ea7cc2f91c5ed85c15e75339662759cfeaeb","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Internal buying and selling prices coordinate decentralized consumption decisions: prosumers adjust their consumption and choose optimal consumption in response to these prices. Scope: Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. An increase in p_s may induce sellers to reduce consumption and thereby increase the energy they sell. Scope: Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal selling price p_s increases. A decrease in p_b may induce buyers to increase consumption and thereby increase the energy they buy. Scope: Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal buying price p_b decreases. The MGO solves the internal-price optimization before distributing the resulting internal prices to all prosumers as coordination signals. Scope: Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C004","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C005","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C006"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"669edd1cfc9a807e4675b5497f63341eb3221c6f1db80e4e555a43d3d0defd6e","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The MGO determines the internal buying and selling prices simultaneously and obtains next-slot prices by solving the pricing optimization. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. The MGO increases the internal selling price p_s in the reported shortage cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. Condition: Selling energy is less than buying energy in these reported time slots. The MGO decreases the internal buying price p_b in the reported surplus cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. Condition: Selling energy is more than buying energy in these reported time slots. Internal buying and selling prices are decision variables for maximizing the MGO's own profit, subject to λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization. Initial internal selling and buying prices may be set to λ^s and λ^b, respectively. Scope: Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. Condition: Initial price setting. Select the internal price pair by comparing MGO profit at the optima of D_1 and D_2, where D_1 applies when E^b \u003c E^s and D_2 applies when E^b ≥ E^s. Scope: Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. The internal selling and buying prices remain at λ^s and λ^b, respectively, in these reported time slots. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. Condition: PV energy is entirely self-consumed and no energy is feasible to trade inside the microgrid.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. | Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. | Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. | Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E11"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C005","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C006","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C008"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"b35948c248279327effe00aef49d47871e55293baf5b4fa11c535f5eaecf835b","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e010","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON INDUSTRIAL INFORMATICS, VOL. 13, NO. 3, JUNE 2017 λb, It can be easily proved t","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"It can be easily proved that the maximum value of U_n is its extremum value. Therefore, with the condition E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0, the extremum value of x_n can be calculated with given prices p_s and p_b: x_n = { k_n/p_s − 1, E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n/p_b − 1, E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (2)","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"It can be easily proved that the maximum value of U_n is its extremum value. Therefore, with the condition E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0, the extremum value of x_n can be calculated with given prices p_s and p_b: x_n = { k_n/p_s − 1, E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n/p_b − 1, E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E06","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"the It only needs to prove the uniqueness of optimized prices pb As and p∗s in order to demonstrate ","equation_id":"(24)-(25)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"By substituting (2) in (3) and (4), we can obtain\nE^{b} = \\frac{\\sum_{n\\in B} k_n}{p_b} - N_B - \\sum_{n\\in B} E_n^g \\quad (24)\nE^{s} = \\sum_{n\\in S} E_n^g - \\frac{\\sum_{n\\in S} k_n}{p_s} + N_S. \\quad (25)\nAs shown in (24) and (25), the total amount of selling energy E^b and buying energy E^s are functions of the internal prices p_b and p_s.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"By substituting (2) in (3) and (4), we can obtain\nE^{b} = \\frac{\\sum_{n\\in B} k_n}{p_b} - N_B - \\sum_{n\\in B} E_n^g \\quad (24)\nE^{s} = \\sum_{n\\in S} E_n^g - \\frac{\\sum_{n\\in S} k_n}{p_s} + N_S. \\quad (25)\nAs shown in (24) and (25), the total amount of selling energy E^b and buying energy E^s are functions of the internal prices p_b and p_s."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.A Formulation of Stackelberg Game","anchor_text":"LIU et al.: ENERGY SHARING MANAGEMENT FOR MICROGRIDS WITH PV PROSUM by changing their energy consump","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e011","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model / II.B Profit Model","anchor_text":"The slot, the initial internal prices ps and pb can be set as λs and red λb, respectively. With the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the increase of p_s, it is possible for seller to decrease the consumption and thus the selling energy will increase. Similarly, with the decrease of p_b, it is possible for buyers to increase the consumption and thus the buying energy will increase. Thus, the role of buyer or seller will not be transformed in response to the setting of internal prices. Hence, although (1) is a piecewise function, and p_b is different from p_s, the utility of a buyer or a seller is the continuously differentiable function of the consumption x_n.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"With the increase of p_s, it is possible for seller to decrease the consumption and thus the selling energy will increase. Similarly, with the decrease of p_b, it is possible for buyers to increase the consumption and thus the buying energy will increase. Thus, the role of buyer or seller will not be transformed in response to the setting of internal prices. Hence, although (1) is a piecewise function, and p_b is different from p_s, the utility of a buyer or a seller is the continuously differentiable function of the consumption x_n."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e019","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.F Analysis of Practical Implementation and Feasibility","anchor_text":"and thus lower the impact on the utility grid. du co F. Analysis of Practical Implementation and Fea","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As the method is implemented by centralized optimization, the prosumers are only required to submit E_n^g, k_n, and role attribute. Meanwhile, the MGO needs to solve problem (30), and then distributes the internal prices p_s and p_b to all the prosumers. Thus, the bidirectional data exchange between MGO and prosumers are only several bytes of data, which can be easily achieved with the monitoring and control system of microgrids.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"As the method is implemented by centralized optimization, the prosumers are only required to submit E_n^g, k_n, and role attribute. Meanwhile, the MGO needs to solve problem (30), and then distributes the internal prices p_s and p_b to all the prosumers. Thus, the bidirectional data exchange between MGO and prosumers are only several bytes of data, which can be easily achieved with the monitoring and control system of microgrids."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e010","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON INDUSTRIAL INFORMATICS, VOL. 13, NO. 3, JUNE 2017 λb, It can be easily proved t","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"It can be easily proved that the maximum value of U_n is its extremum value. Therefore, with the condition E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0, the extremum value of x_n can be calculated with given prices p_s and p_b: x_n = { k_n/p_s − 1, E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n/p_b − 1, E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (2)","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"It can be easily proved that the maximum value of U_n is its extremum value. Therefore, with the condition E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0, the extremum value of x_n can be calculated with given prices p_s and p_b: x_n = { k_n/p_s − 1, E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n/p_b − 1, E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e019","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.B Analysis of the Internal Prices","anchor_text":"en re Fig. 9. Comparison of net energy. is D First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount of selling energy is less than the buying energy, the MGO increases the selling price p_{s} and motivates the sellers to sell more energy; and second, in time slots 13 and 14, as the amount of selling energy is more than the buying energy, the MGO decreases the buying price p_{b}, and thus the buyers are encouraged to consume more extra PV energy.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount of selling energy is less than the buying energy, the MGO increases the selling price p_{s} and motivates the sellers to sell more energy; and second, in time slots 13 and 14, as the amount of selling energy is more than the buying energy, the MGO decreases the buying price p_{b}, and thus the buyers are encouraged to consume more extra PV energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e008","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON INDUSTRIAL INFORMATICS, VOL. 13, NO. 3, JUNE 2017 λb, It can be easily proved t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For each time slot, the initial internal prices p_s and p_b can be set as λ^s and λ^b, respectively.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"For each time slot, the initial internal prices p_s and p_b can be set as λ^s and λ^b, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p10-c1r2__v141-a-M01-validation","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"sel s.t. λs ≤pb ≤λb, λs ≤ps ≤λb, Eb ≥Es. (27) con Therefore, from (26) and (27), considering the rel","equation_id":"(28)-(29)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Therefore, from (26) and (27), considering the relationship between E^b and E^s, the feasible region of p_b and p_s can be divided into two parts: D_1 and D_2. If E^b \u003c E^s, then (p_b, p_s) \\in D_1. Otherwise, if E^b \\ge E^s, then (p_b, p_s) \\in D_2. Finally, we have that D_1 and D_2 meet the following conditions:\nD_1 \\cup D_2 = D, \\quad D_1 \\cap D_2 = \\phi. \\quad (28)","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Therefore, from (26) and (27), considering the relationship between E^b and E^s, the feasible region of p_b and p_s can be divided into two parts: D_1 and D_2. If E^b \u003c E^s, then (p_b, p_s) \\in D_1. Otherwise, if E^b \\ge E^s, then (p_b, p_s) \\in D_2. Finally, we have that D_1 and D_2 meet the following conditions:\nD_1 \\cup D_2 = D, \\quad D_1 \\cap D_2 = \\phi. \\quad (28)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p10-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"we have the Hessian matrix H that is negative deﬁnite with [3 respect to pb and ps. Thereby, R is th","equation_id":"(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The optimal internal prices of the MGO is existence and uniqueness in D_1 and D_2, which are (p_{bD_1}^*, p_{sD_1}^*) and (p_{bD_2}^*, p_{sD_2}^*), respectively. From (28), we note that the optimal internal prices in D can be represented as follows\n(p_b^*, p_s^*) = \\operatorname*{argmax}_{(p_b,p_s)}\\left(R(p_{bD_1}^*, p_{sD_1}^*), R(p_{bD_2}^*, p_{sD_2}^*)\\right). \\quad (30)\nThen we have that the optimal internal prices (p_b^*, p_s^*) is unique. Thus, there exists a unique SE and Theorem 1 is proved.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"The optimal internal prices of the MGO is existence and uniqueness in D_1 and D_2, which are (p_{bD_1}^*, p_{sD_1}^*) and (p_{bD_2}^*, p_{sD_2}^*), respectively. From (28), we note that the optimal internal prices in D can be represented as follows\n(p_b^*, p_s^*) = \\operatorname*{argmax}_{(p_b,p_s)}\\left(R(p_{bD_1}^*, p_{sD_1}^*), R(p_{bD_2}^*, p_{sD_2}^*)\\right). \\quad (30)\nThen we have that the optimal internal prices (p_b^*, p_s^*) is unique. Thus, there exists a unique SE and Theorem 1 is proved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.A Basic Data","anchor_text":"y g gy, g gy, ergy consumption of the microgrid in each time slot are shown in Fig. 5. Fig B. Analys","equation_id":"(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"By using the basic data of the five prosumers, the SE of energy sharing game on every time slot can be achieved by solving (30). The internal prices of every time slot during the daytime are shown in Fig. 6. In time slots 7, 17-19, the internal prices are shown equally with the \\lambda^{s} and \\lambda^{b}. This is due to the fact that as the PV energy are all self-consumed by each prosumers, there is no more energy that is feasible to be traded inside the microgrid. Hence, the internal prices are constant with \\lambda^{s} and \\lambda^{b}.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"By using the basic data of the five prosumers, the SE of energy sharing game on every time slot can be achieved by solving (30). The internal prices of every time slot during the daytime are shown in Fig. 6. In time slots 7, 17-19, the internal prices are shown equally with the \\lambda^{s} and \\lambda^{b}. This is due to the fact that as the PV energy are all self-consumed by each prosumers, there is no more energy that is feasible to be traded inside the microgrid. Hence, the internal prices are constant with \\lambda^{s} and \\lambda^{b}."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["operator_profit_optimal_price_pair"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"KG31-L6-SC-L6-4447ef62f8f5eec2","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L6","ontological_kind":"SC-L6-4447ef62f8f5eec2"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"Treats the unit prices on the internal purchase and sale sides as a joint decision, maximizing the operator's profit in combination with participant price response, external surplus-deficit trading, and price constraints, thereby forming an optimal price pair shared by each side within the region.","identity_fields":["Function: jointly optimize to generate internal purchase and sale prices","Price structure: the internal purchase side and sale side each share one price","Economic principle: maximization of operator profit accounting for consumption response and external balance trading"]},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","paper_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"The MGO coordinates and optimizes local PV energy sharing with the objective of maximizing its own profit. Scope: Hour-ahead energy-sharing management among PV prosumers within one microgrid. The internal prices p_b and p_s determine the aggregate trading quantities E^b and E^s through the model's price-dependent consumption responses. Scope: Determination of aggregate local trading quantities in the Stackelberg energy-sharing model. Condition: Trading quantities use the consumption response in (2), derived under E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0. The final ESM decision may be scheduled five minutes before the time slot. Scope: Implementation timing of the final local energy-sharing decision for a forthcoming time slot. Condition: The monitoring and control system's communication latency is commonly less than several seconds.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Determination of aggregate local trading quantities in the Stackelberg energy-sharing model. | Hour-ahead energy-sharing management among PV prosumers within one microgrid. | Implementation timing of the final local energy-sharing decision for a forthcoming time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E06"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C004"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"3a304bae600d1d987d8d474ca346ea7cc2f91c5ed85c15e75339662759cfeaeb"},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Internal buying and selling prices coordinate decentralized consumption decisions: prosumers adjust their consumption and choose optimal consumption in response to these prices. Scope: Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. An increase in p_s may induce sellers to reduce consumption and thereby increase the energy they sell. Scope: Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal selling price p_s increases. A decrease in p_b may induce buyers to increase consumption and thereby increase the energy they buy. Scope: Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal buying price p_b decreases. The MGO solves the internal-price optimization before distributing the resulting internal prices to all prosumers as coordination signals. Scope: Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C004","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C005","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C006"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"669edd1cfc9a807e4675b5497f63341eb3221c6f1db80e4e555a43d3d0defd6e"},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The MGO determines the internal buying and selling prices simultaneously and obtains next-slot prices by solving the pricing optimization. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. The MGO increases the internal selling price p_s in the reported shortage cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. Condition: Selling energy is less than buying energy in these reported time slots. The MGO decreases the internal buying price p_b in the reported surplus cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. Condition: Selling energy is more than buying energy in these reported time slots. Internal buying and selling prices are decision variables for maximizing the MGO's own profit, subject to λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization. Initial internal selling and buying prices may be set to λ^s and λ^b, respectively. Scope: Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. Condition: Initial price setting. Select the internal price pair by comparing MGO profit at the optima of D_1 and D_2, where D_1 applies when E^b \u003c E^s and D_2 applies when E^b ≥ E^s. Scope: Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. The internal selling and buying prices remain at λ^s and λ^b, respectively, in these reported time slots. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. Condition: PV energy is entirely self-consumed and no energy is feasible to trade inside the microgrid.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. | Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. | Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. | Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E11"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C005","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C006","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C008"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"b35948c248279327effe00aef49d47871e55293baf5b4fa11c535f5eaecf835b"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The internal prices p_b and p_s determine the aggregate trading quantities E^b and E^s through the model's price-dependent consumption responses. Scope: Determination of aggregate local trading quantities in the Stackelberg energy-sharing model. Condition: Trading quantities use the consumption response in (2), derived under E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0.","expression":"E^{b} = \\frac{\\sum_{n\\in B} k_n}{p_b} - N_B - \\sum_{n\\in B} E_n^g \\quad (24)\nE^{s} = \\sum_{n\\in S} E_n^g - \\frac{\\sum_{n\\in S} k_n}{p_s} + N_S. \\quad (25)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-xn","v141-c-R002-Eb","v141-c-R002-Es"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R002-pb","v141-c-R002-ps","v141-c-R002-kn","v141-c-R002-Eng","v141-c-R002-NB","v141-c-R002-NS"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g03-E06"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e010","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON INDUSTRIAL INFORMATICS, VOL. 13, NO. 3, JUNE 2017 λb, It can be easily proved t","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"It can be easily proved that the maximum value of U_n is its extremum value. Therefore, with the condition E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0, the extremum value of x_n can be calculated with given prices p_s and p_b: x_n = { k_n/p_s − 1, E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n/p_b − 1, E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E06","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"the It only needs to prove the uniqueness of optimized prices pb As and p∗s in order to demonstrate ","equation_id":"(24)-(25)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"By substituting (2) in (3) and (4), we can obtain\nE^{b} = \\frac{\\sum_{n\\in B} k_n}{p_b} - N_B - \\sum_{n\\in B} E_n^g \\quad (24)\nE^{s} = \\sum_{n\\in S} E_n^g - \\frac{\\sum_{n\\in S} k_n}{p_s} + N_S. \\quad (25)\nAs shown in (24) and (25), the total amount of selling energy E^b and buying energy E^s are functions of the internal prices p_b and p_s."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Given internal prices p_s and p_b, the extremum value of x_n is given by (2), with the condition E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0.","expression":"x_n = \\begin{cases} k_n/p_s - 1, & E_n^g - x_n > 0; \\\\ k_n/p_b - 1, & E_n^g - x_n \\le 0, \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{under } E_n^g - x_n \\ne 0.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-xn"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R002-ps","v141-c-R002-pb","v141-c-R002-kn","v141-c-R002-Eng"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e010","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON INDUSTRIAL INFORMATICS, VOL. 13, NO. 3, JUNE 2017 λb, It can be easily proved t","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"It can be easily proved that the maximum value of U_n is its extremum value. Therefore, with the condition E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0, the extremum value of x_n can be calculated with given prices p_s and p_b: x_n = { k_n/p_s − 1, E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n/p_b − 1, E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (2)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Internal buying and selling prices coordinate decentralized consumption decisions: prosumers adjust their consumption and choose optimal consumption in response to these prices. Scope: Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e015"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.A Formulation of Stackelberg Game","anchor_text":"LIU et al.: ENERGY SHARING MANAGEMENT FOR MICROGRIDS WITH PV PROSUM by changing their energy consump","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"An increase in p_s may induce sellers to reduce consumption and thereby increase the energy they sell. Scope: Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal selling price p_s increases.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e011","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model / II.B Profit Model","anchor_text":"The slot, the initial internal prices ps and pb can be set as λs and red λb, respectively. With the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the increase of p_s, it is possible for seller to decrease the consumption and thus the selling energy will increase. Similarly, with the decrease of p_b, it is possible for buyers to increase the consumption and thus the buying energy will increase. Thus, the role of buyer or seller will not be transformed in response to the setting of internal prices. Hence, although (1) is a piecewise function, and p_b is different from p_s, the utility of a buyer or a seller is the continuously differentiable function of the consumption x_n."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A decrease in p_b may induce buyers to increase consumption and thereby increase the energy they buy. Scope: Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal buying price p_b decreases.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e011","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model / II.B Profit Model","anchor_text":"The slot, the initial internal prices ps and pb can be set as λs and red λb, respectively. With the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the increase of p_s, it is possible for seller to decrease the consumption and thus the selling energy will increase. Similarly, with the decrease of p_b, it is possible for buyers to increase the consumption and thus the buying energy will increase. Thus, the role of buyer or seller will not be transformed in response to the setting of internal prices. Hence, although (1) is a piecewise function, and p_b is different from p_s, the utility of a buyer or a seller is the continuously differentiable function of the consumption x_n."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO solves the internal-price optimization before distributing the resulting internal prices to all prosumers as coordination signals. Scope: Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e019","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.F Analysis of Practical Implementation and Feasibility","anchor_text":"and thus lower the impact on the utility grid. du co F. Analysis of Practical Implementation and Fea","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As the method is implemented by centralized optimization, the prosumers are only required to submit E_n^g, k_n, and role attribute. Meanwhile, the MGO needs to solve problem (30), and then distributes the internal prices p_s and p_b to all the prosumers. Thus, the bidirectional data exchange between MGO and prosumers are only several bytes of data, which can be easily achieved with the monitoring and control system of microgrids."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"With given internal prices p_s and p_b and E_n^g - x_n ≠ 0, the prosumer's extremum energy consumption is x_n = k_n/p_s - 1 when E_n^g - x_n > 0, and x_n = k_n/p_b - 1 when E_n^g - x_n ≤ 0. Scope: Prosumer best-response consumption to internal price signals in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","expression":"x_n = { k_n/p_s - 1, if E_n^g - x_n > 0; k_n/p_b - 1, if E_n^g - x_n ≤ 0 }, subject to E_n^g - x_n ≠ 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R004-x001","v141-c-R004-x002","v141-c-R004-x003"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R004-t001","v141-c-R004-t002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e010","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON INDUSTRIAL INFORMATICS, VOL. 13, NO. 3, JUNE 2017 λb, It can be easily proved t","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"It can be easily proved that the maximum value of U_n is its extremum value. Therefore, with the condition E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0, the extremum value of x_n can be calculated with given prices p_s and p_b: x_n = { k_n/p_s − 1, E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n/p_b − 1, E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e011","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model / II.B Profit Model","anchor_text":"The slot, the initial internal prices ps and pb can be set as λs and red λb, respectively. With the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the increase of p_s, it is possible for seller to decrease the consumption and thus the selling energy will increase. Similarly, with the decrease of p_b, it is possible for buyers to increase the consumption and thus the buying energy will increase. Thus, the role of buyer or seller will not be transformed in response to the setting of internal prices. Hence, although (1) is a piecewise function, and p_b is different from p_s, the utility of a buyer or a seller is the continuously differentiable function of the consumption x_n."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.A Formulation of Stackelberg Game","anchor_text":"LIU et al.: ENERGY SHARING MANAGEMENT FOR MICROGRIDS WITH PV PROSUM by changing their energy consump","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C006","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Internal price signals satisfy the source's p.3 ordering λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. Page 4 prints the upper bound as λ^b_n, and Appendix (26) states non-strict two-sided price bounds; this is an unresolved source variant.","expression":"λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R004-x002","v141-c-R004-x003"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R004-t003","v141-c-R004-t004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e015"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.A Formulation of Stackelberg Game","anchor_text":"LIU et al.: ENERGY SHARING MANAGEMENT FOR MICROGRIDS WITH PV PROSUM by changing their energy consump","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO determines the internal buying and selling prices simultaneously and obtains next-slot prices by solving the pricing optimization. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e019"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e019","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO increases the internal selling price p_s in the reported shortage cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. Condition: Selling energy is less than buying energy in these reported time slots.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E12"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.B Analysis of the Internal Prices","anchor_text":"en re Fig. 9. Comparison of net energy. is D First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount of selling energy is less than the buying energy, the MGO increases the selling price p_{s} and motivates the sellers to sell more energy; and second, in time slots 13 and 14, as the amount of selling energy is more than the buying energy, the MGO decreases the buying price p_{b}, and thus the buyers are encouraged to consume more extra PV energy."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO decreases the internal buying price p_b in the reported surplus cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. Condition: Selling energy is more than buying energy in these reported time slots.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E12"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.B Analysis of the Internal Prices","anchor_text":"en re Fig. 9. Comparison of net energy. is D First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount of selling energy is less than the buying energy, the MGO increases the selling price p_{s} and motivates the sellers to sell more energy; and second, in time slots 13 and 14, as the amount of selling energy is more than the buying energy, the MGO decreases the buying price p_{b}, and thus the buyers are encouraged to consume more extra PV energy."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Internal buying and selling prices are decision variables for maximizing the MGO's own profit, subject to λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization.","expression":"\\max_{p_b,p_s} R(p_b,p_s)\\quad \\text{s.t.}\\quad \\lambda^s \\le p_s \u003c p_b \\le \\lambda^b,\\quad R(p_b,p_s)=\\begin{cases} p_b E^b - p_s E^s + \\lambda^s(E^s-E^b), & E^s>E^b,\\\\ p_b E^b - p_s E^s + \\lambda^b(E^s-E^b), & E^s\\le E^b. \\end{cases}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_p_b","x_p_s"],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_s","theta_lambda_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e014"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Initial internal selling and buying prices may be set to λ^s and λ^b, respectively. Scope: Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. Condition: Initial price setting.","expression":"p_s = \\lambda^s,\\quad p_b = \\lambda^b \\quad \\text{(initialization for each time slot)}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_p_s","x_p_b"],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_s","theta_lambda_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e008"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e008","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON INDUSTRIAL INFORMATICS, VOL. 13, NO. 3, JUNE 2017 λb, It can be easily proved t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For each time slot, the initial internal prices p_s and p_b can be set as λ^s and λ^b, respectively."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C006","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Select the internal price pair by comparing MGO profit at the optima of D_1 and D_2, where D_1 applies when E^b \u003c E^s and D_2 applies when E^b ≥ E^s. Scope: Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions.","expression":"(p_b^*,p_s^*) = \\operatorname*{argmax}_{(p_b,p_s)}\\left(R(p_{bD_1}^*,p_{sD_1}^*), R(p_{bD_2}^*,p_{sD_2}^*)\\right),\\quad (p_b,p_s)\\in D_1 \\text{ if } E^b\u003cE^s,\\; (p_b,p_s)\\in D_2 \\text{ if } E^b\\ge E^s","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_p_b","x_p_s"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E11"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p10-c1r2__v141-a-M01-validation","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"sel s.t. λs ≤pb ≤λb, λs ≤ps ≤λb, Eb ≥Es. (27) con Therefore, from (26) and (27), considering the rel","equation_id":"(28)-(29)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Therefore, from (26) and (27), considering the relationship between E^b and E^s, the feasible region of p_b and p_s can be divided into two parts: D_1 and D_2. If E^b \u003c E^s, then (p_b, p_s) \\in D_1. Otherwise, if E^b \\ge E^s, then (p_b, p_s) \\in D_2. Finally, we have that D_1 and D_2 meet the following conditions:\nD_1 \\cup D_2 = D, \\quad D_1 \\cap D_2 = \\phi. \\quad (28)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p10-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"we have the Hessian matrix H that is negative deﬁnite with [3 respect to pb and ps. Thereby, R is th","equation_id":"(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The optimal internal prices of the MGO is existence and uniqueness in D_1 and D_2, which are (p_{bD_1}^*, p_{sD_1}^*) and (p_{bD_2}^*, p_{sD_2}^*), respectively. From (28), we note that the optimal internal prices in D can be represented as follows\n(p_b^*, p_s^*) = \\operatorname*{argmax}_{(p_b,p_s)}\\left(R(p_{bD_1}^*, p_{sD_1}^*), R(p_{bD_2}^*, p_{sD_2}^*)\\right). \\quad (30)\nThen we have that the optimal internal prices (p_b^*, p_s^*) is unique. Thus, there exists a unique SE and Theorem 1 is proved."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C007","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The internal selling and buying prices remain at λ^s and λ^b, respectively, in these reported time slots. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. Condition: PV energy is entirely self-consumed and no energy is feasible to trade inside the microgrid.","expression":"\\forall t\\in\\{7,17,18,19\\}:\\; p_s(t)=\\lambda^s,\\; p_b(t)=\\lambda^b \\quad \\text{when PV energy is entirely self-consumed and no internal trade is feasible}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_p_s","x_p_b"],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_s","theta_lambda_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.A Basic Data","anchor_text":"y g gy, g gy, ergy consumption of the microgrid in each time slot are shown in Fig. 5. Fig B. Analys","equation_id":"(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"By using the basic data of the five prosumers, the SE of energy sharing game on every time slot can be achieved by solving (30). The internal prices of every time slot during the daytime are shown in Fig. 6. In time slots 7, 17-19, the internal prices are shown equally with the \\lambda^{s} and \\lambda^{b}. This is due to the fact that as the PV energy are all self-consumed by each prosumers, there is no more energy that is feasible to be traded inside the microgrid. Hence, the internal prices are constant with \\lambda^{s} and \\lambda^{b}."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C008","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The MGO profit objective for internal-price optimization is the piecewise function R(p_b,p_s) in (5): it collects p_b E^b from buyers and pays p_s E^s to sellers, and settles the net imbalance with the utility grid at λ^s when E^s > E^b or at λ^b when E^s ≤ E^b. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization.","expression":"R(p_b,p_s)=\\begin{cases} p_b E^b - p_s E^s + \\lambda^s(E^s-E^b), & E^s>E^b,\\\\ p_b E^b - p_s E^s + \\lambda^b(E^s-E^b), & E^s\\le E^b. \\end{cases}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["x_p_b","x_p_s"],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_s","theta_lambda_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e007"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-xn","symbol":"x_n","meaning":"Energy consumed by prosumer n in one time slot; the source calls x_n the prosumer's ESM decision variable.","kind":"operational","domain":"x_n^{min} ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^{max}","unit":null,"indices":["n ∈ G"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e015"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-xn"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-Eb","symbol":"E^b","meaning":"Total trading energy of buyers, defined over the buyer set B as Σ_{n∈B}(x_n − E_n^g); Appendix A prose labels E^b as 'selling energy', an ambiguity preserved rather than silently swapped.","kind":"operational","domain":"aggregate energy quantity; no independent numeric domain is stated beyond the source definitions","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g03-E06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-Eb"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-Es","symbol":"E^s","meaning":"Total trading energy of sellers, defined over the seller set S as Σ_{n∈S}(E_n^g − x_n); Appendix A prose labels E^s as 'buying energy', an ambiguity preserved rather than silently swapped.","kind":"operational","domain":"aggregate energy quantity; no independent numeric domain is stated beyond the source definitions","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g03-E06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-Es"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R004-x001","symbol":"x_n","meaning":"Energy consumed by prosumer n in one time slot; the prosumer's decision variable in the Stackelberg ESM, adjusted in response to internal prices.","kind":"operational","domain":"x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max","unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e015"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x001"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R004-x002","symbol":"p_s","meaning":"Internal selling price set by the MGO as the leader's price signal; treated as given by prosumer n when choosing consumption.","kind":"operational","domain":"λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b","unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e019"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x002"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R004-x003","symbol":"p_b","meaning":"Internal buying price set by the MGO as the leader's price signal; treated as given by prosumer n when choosing consumption.","kind":"operational","domain":"λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b","unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e019"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x003"},{"variable_id":"x_p_s","symbol":"p_s","meaning":"Internal selling price set by the MGO for the next time slot; a decision variable in the MGO profit-maximization and bounded by the internal-price constraint.","kind":"operational","domain":"real scalar per time slot; λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b","unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":["time slot"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::x::x_p_s"},{"variable_id":"x_p_b","symbol":"p_b","meaning":"Internal buying price set by the MGO for the next time slot; a decision variable in the MGO profit-maximization and bounded by the internal-price constraint.","kind":"operational","domain":"real scalar per time slot; λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b","unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":["time slot"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::x::x_p_b"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-pb","symbol":"p_b","meaning":"Internal buying price set by the MGO; treated as a price input to the clearing response in this rule and as an MGO decision variable in the pricing problem.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e014"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-pb"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-ps","symbol":"p_s","meaning":"Internal selling price set by the MGO; treated as a price input to the clearing response in this rule and as an MGO decision variable in the pricing problem.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e014"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-ps"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-kn","symbol":"k_n","meaning":"Preference parameter of prosumer n; enters the piecewise consumption response and hence the aggregate clearing quantities.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n ∈ G"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e010"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-kn"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-Eng","symbol":"E_n^g","meaning":"Energy produced by prosumer n in one time slot.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n ∈ G"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-Eng"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-NB","symbol":"N_B","meaning":"Number of buyers, N_B = |B|.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-NB"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-NS","symbol":"N_S","meaning":"Number of sellers, N_S = |S|.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-NS"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-t001","symbol":"k_n","meaning":"Preference parameter of prosumer n; positive in the source's response and concavity conditions.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"k_n > 0"},"unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g03-E10"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t001"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-t002","symbol":"E_n^g","meaning":"Energy produced by prosumer n in one time slot; treated as given in the net-trade term E_n^g - x_n and in the consumption response.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"E_n^g"},"unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t002"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-t003","symbol":"λ^s","meaning":"Utility-grid export price, constant in the source; lower bound for the internal selling price in the price ordering. The case study sets 0.4 CNY/kWh.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"λ^s"},"unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g02-E01"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t003"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-t004","symbol":"λ^b","meaning":"Utility-grid import price, constant in the source; upper bound for the internal buying price in the price ordering. The case study sets 1.0 CNY/kWh.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"λ^b"},"unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g02-E01"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t004"},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_s","symbol":"λ^s","meaning":"Utility-grid export (feed-in) price; constant export price, lower than import price λ^b. Case-study calibration λ^s = 0.4 CNY/kWh.","value":{"kind":"numeric","number_value":0.4,"text_value":null},"unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g02-E01"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_s"},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_b","symbol":"λ^b","meaning":"Utility-grid import price; constant import price, higher than export price λ^s. Case-study calibration λ^b = 1.0 CNY/kWh.","value":{"kind":"numeric","number_value":1.0,"text_value":null},"unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g02-E01"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_b"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","stage":"L6","subtype":"operator_profit_optimal_price_pair","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The MGO simultaneously selects p_b and p_s to maximize R(p_b,p_s); the main-text constraint is λ^s≤p_s\u003cp_b≤λ^b. R is p_bE^b−p_sE^s+λ^s(E^s−E^b) when E^s>E^b, and otherwise p_bE^b−p_sE^s+λ^b(E^s−E^b); comparing the profits at the respective optimal points of D_1 and D_2 determines the final price pair.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: internal electricity purchase and sale unit price pair","Core operation: maximize operator profit under price constraints, incorporating consumption response and external balance trading","Output: optimal internal prices (p_b^*,p_s^*)"],"variation_fields":["D_1 corresponds to E^b\u003cE^s, and D_2 corresponds to E^b≥E^s; implementation may use an interior-point method and broadcast the price for the next time slot","Transaction quantities adopt the source text's price response; the extreme-value response in equation (2) requires E_n^g−x_n≠0, and the consumption strategy has separate upper and lower bounds","Initial prices may be set to p_s=λ^s and p_b=λ^b; the case grid prices are 0.4 and 1.0 CNY/kWh","The strict price spread in the main text, another upper bound on λ^b_n, and the non-strict two-sided bounds in the appendix are retained as different source-text formulations","In the case, during shortage in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, p_s is raised; during surplus in 13 and 14, p_b is lowered; this is not extended into a general adjustment algorithm","In the case, when there is no internally tradable electricity in time slots 7 and 17-19, the prices remain at the grid prices"],"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C005","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C006","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C005","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C006","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007"],"paper_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","template_code":"PGR"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","retained_variants":["The MGO simultaneously selects p_b and p_s to maximize R(p_b,p_s); the main-text constraint is λ^s≤p_s\u003cp_b≤λ^b.","When E^s>E^b, R=p_bE^b−p_sE^s+λ^s(E^s−E^b); otherwise R=p_bE^b−p_sE^s+λ^b(E^s−E^b).","D_1 corresponds to E^b\u003cE^s, and D_2 corresponds to E^b≥E^s; comparing the profits at the optimal points in the two domains determines (p_b^*,p_s^*).","Implementation may use an interior-point method and broadcast the price for the next time slot; transaction quantities adopt the source text's price response.","The extreme-value response in equation (2) requires E_n^g−x_n≠0, and the consumption strategy has separate upper and lower bounds.","Initial prices may be set to p_s=λ^s and p_b=λ^b; the case grid prices are 0.4 and 1.0 CNY/kWh.","The strict price spread in the main text, another upper bound on λ^b_n, and the non-strict two-sided bounds in the appendix are retained separately and are not uniformly rewritten.","In the case, during shortage in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, p_s is raised; during surplus in 13 and 14, p_b is lowered; this is not extended into a general adjustment algorithm.","In the case, when there is no internally tradable electricity in time slots 7 and 17-19, the prices remain at the grid prices."],"evidence_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local::projection"]}],"functional":{"is_child":true,"subdivision_pending":false,"baseline_parent_id":"COMP-9510de1f159cf644","baseline_parent_code":"PRC019","secondary_class":"SC-L6-4447ef62f8f5eec2","category":{"id":"SC-L6-4447ef62f8f5eec2","stage":"L6","label_zh":"Operator-profit-optimal two-sided pricing","definition_zh":"The operator, incorporating participant price response and external surplus-deficit trading, jointly selects the unit prices shared on the internal purchase and sale sides under price constraints in order to maximize its own profit.","main_identity_axes":["Function: jointly optimize to generate a purchase and sale price pair","Price structure: within the shared region, common pricing is applied separately to the purchase and sale sides","Economic principle: response-coupled maximization of operator profit"],"inclusion_criteria":["Both the internal purchase price and sale price are price decisions selected by the operator.","The profit objective accounts for both internal transactions and external surplus-deficit transactions.","Transaction quantities or consumption behavior respond to the selected prices."],"exclusion_criteria":["Balance and allocate external transaction revenue and expenditure according to a fixed supply-demand formula.","Use social welfare, buyer savings, or balancing dual values as the pricing objective or basis.","There is only one common price within the domain, and no purchase-side and sale-side price pair is formed.","Only apply, retain, or publish already determined prices."],"supporting_unit_ids":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local"],"status":"agent_defined_structurally_validated"},"definition":{"definition_zh":"Treats the unit prices on the internal purchase and sale sides as a joint decision, maximizing the operator's profit in combination with participant price response, external surplus-deficit trading, and price constraints, thereby forming an optimal price pair shared by each side within the region.","identity_fields":["Function: jointly optimize to generate internal purchase and sale prices","Price structure: the internal purchase side and sale side each share one price","Economic principle: maximization of operator profit accounting for consumption response and external balance trading"],"member_unit_ids":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local"]}},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/319"});
